<title>SRI LANKA: Three Acre buys piggery, hatchery firm.</title>
<headline>Three Acre buys piggery, hatchery firm.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Acre Farms Ltd, a supplier of day-old chicks, has agreed in principle to buy unlisted firm Christombu Farms for 280 million rupees to diversify its operations, a Three Acre statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Christombu Farms owns a piggery, hatchery and 10 retail outlets.</p>
<p>Nandakumar Nair, head of research at brokerage John Keells, said he understood 175 million rupees of the total sum would be paid in cash, with the balance to be met by issuing 2.1 million Three Acre shares at 50 rupees to the owners of Christombu Farms. Three Acre shares last traded at 27.25 rupees.</p>
</text>
